# Using Codex in {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## What loads automatically

- Root `AGENTS.md` is the project instruction entrypoint.
- Repository skills under `.agents/skills` are discoverable by name and description.
- A full `SKILL.md` loads when explicitly invoked or when its description matches the task.
- Other docs are read on demand through `AGENTS.md`; they are not all loaded for every task.

## Daily workflow

```text
Define the task with docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md
                ↓
Use a matching project skill or execute the scoped task
                ↓
$build-and-test
                ↓
$code-review
```

### Feature

```text
Use docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md to define this feature.
Inspect the current repository and propose a plan with files, interfaces, non-goals,
acceptance criteria, and verification. Do not edit until the plan is approved.
```

### Verification

```text
Use $build-and-test. Verify the current diff and report every command as
pass, fail, or not run, including remaining risk.
```

### Review

```text
Use $code-review. Review the current diff and report findings first.
Do not modify files.
```

## Project-specific commands

See `docs/VERIFICATION.md`. Model choice is manual; project docs and skills do not switch the active model.
